        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "It is in the graveyard that Hamlet finally realizes that the inevitable end of life is the grave and clay and that the end of all pretentiousness and all plotting and counter-plotting, regardless of one's station in life, must be dust.",
